   "text": "This looks like cefotetan, read from the drawing as follows.\n\n- **Left side:** a 1-methyltetrazol-5-yl group, joined through S\u2013CH2 to the dihydrothiazine ring of the cephem core. The ring carbon bearing this CH2S group is double-bonded to the carbon carrying the COOH.\n- **Core:** a \u03b2-lactam fused to the six-membered S-containing ring. The carbon next to the lactam C=O carries OMe and the NH, and the NH bond is hashed.\n- **Ring-fusion carbon:** it carries a wedged H.\n- **Right side:** the NH is acylated by a 1,3-dithietane-2-carbonyl group. The dithietane is 4-ylidene, double-bonded to a carbon bearing COOH and CONH2.\n\nFor the two stereocentres, I assigned the C7 (OMe/NH) and C6 (H) configurations from the hash and wedge geometry. The dithietane CH and the ylidene double bond are drawn without stereo marks, so I left them unspecified.\n\nSMILES: CO[C@@]1(NC(=O)C2SC(=C(C(N)=O)C(=O)O)S2)C(=O)N2C(C(=O)O)=C(CSc3nnnn3C)CS[C@H]12"
